{
  // Dependency-vulnerability gate for CI (replaces the bare `npm audit --audit-level=high`,
  // which has no way to record a reasoned exception).
  //
  // The gate stays sharp: anything high/critical that is NOT listed below fails the build.
  // `allowlist` is per-advisory (GHSA id), never per-severity — we do not lower the level.
  //
  // Adding an entry requires, in this file: (1) the advisory id, (2) why it does not apply to
  // THIS codebase, measured — not assumed, (3) an expiry date, (4) what removes the need for it.
  // An expired entry is a task, not a renewal: re-check it, do not extend it by reflex.
  //
  // Take the fix first. Of the four high advisories open against this tree on 2026-07-29, two
  // were closed by a version bump (postcss 8.5.24, react-router-dom 7.18.1) and two had no
  // adoptable fix. On 2026-08-04 one of those two, GHSA-mh99-v99m-4gvg (brace-expansion), got
  // one: upstream published 1.1.18 and 2.1.4, which is exactly the "no patched 1.x / no patched
  // 2.x" measurement the entry rested on. It was deleted, not renewed — together with the two
  // new advisories of that wave (GHSA-rgw5-rvv9-x895, GHSA-7p8r-x3mc-p8w7), which were also
  // closed by bumping. Net effect of #148: one entry removed, zero added.
  // Policy: docs/development/dependency-audit.md
  "$schema": "https://github.com/IBM/audit-ci/raw/main/docs/schema.json",
  "moderate": false,
  "high": true,
  "critical": true,
  "allowlist": [
    // GHSA-qwww-vcr4-c8h2 — react-router "RSC Mode CSRF Bypass Allows Action Execution Before
    // 400 Response" (high). Vulnerable range 7.12.0–8.2.0; there is NO fix in the 7.x line
    // (react-router-dom stops at 7.18.1; the fix is react-router v8 >= 8.3.0, a different
    // package and a breaking upgrade).
    //
    // Why it does not apply here (measured 2026-07-29 on this tree):
    //   - `src/app/router.tsx` builds the whole route table with `createBrowserRouter` and
    //     **element-only** route objects. A grep for route-level `action:` / `loader:` keys
    //     across `src/` returns 0 hits, so there is no route action for a server to execute.
    //   - All 17 react-router call sites import from `react-router-dom` (the client package).
    //     `@react-router/dev`, `react-router/rsc`, `createStaticHandler` and
    //     `StaticRouterProvider` appear 0 times in `src/` and in `package.json` — no RSC mode,
    //     no server components, no framework-mode server runtime.
    //   - `vite.config.ts` builds to `outDir: ../public_html/admin` — a **static SPA bundle**
    //     served as files. There is no server that could run a route action before returning 400.
    // The advisory's attack path has no counterpart in a client-only bundle.
    //
    // Expiry: 2026-08-31. Removed by the react-router v8 migration wave (bundled with the
    // NENE2 RR8 re-evaluation). If that wave slips past the expiry, the entry must be
    // re-argued in a PR — not silently extended.
    "GHSA-qwww-vcr4-c8h2",
  ],
}
